    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q57-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\cot\\theta-2\\cot 2\\theta=\\tan\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cot\\theta-2\\cot 2\\theta=\\tan\\theta$.\n\nReplace $\\cot 2\\theta$ using the reciprocal of the tangent double-angle formula.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{LHS}&=\\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta}-2\\left(\\frac{1-\\tan^2\\theta}{2\\tan\\theta}\\right)\\\\\\text{LHS}&=\\frac{1-(1-\\tan^2\\theta)}{\\tan\\theta}\\\\\\text{LHS}&=\\tan\\theta\\\\\\text{LHS}&=\\text{RHS}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q57-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, simplify\n\n$$\\tan x+2\\tan 2x+4\\tan 4x+\\cdots+2^n\\tan(2^n x).$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\cot x-2^{n+1}\\cot(2^{n+1}x)$.\n\nApply part a to successive doubled arguments; the intermediate cotangent terms cancel.",
          "worked": "By part a,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan x&=\\cot x-2\\cot 2x\\\\2\\tan 2x&=2\\cot 2x-4\\cot 4x\\\\4\\tan 4x&=4\\cot 4x-8\\cot 8x\\\\2^n\\tan(2^n x)&=2^n\\cot(2^n x)-2^{n+1}\\cot(2^{n+1}x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdding these and all intervening terms cancels the intermediate cotangent terms. Therefore the sum is\n\n$$\\cot x-2^{n+1}\\cot(2^{n+1}x).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
  },
